# Which absence reasons each question has ever taken, as a three-bit word. One row per question,
# the mask reading `n u a` for none, unmeasured and notApplicable, and a dot where the corpus has
# never used that reason.
#
# Reached states as a word
#   `AbsenceReason` is three members, so a site's reached states are a word rather than a list,
#   and that is the whole trick. Asked as rows, "which reasons does `remainder sign` file" is a pile
#   of rows nobody reads. Asked as a word it reads like `.ua`, and it sits beside `boundOrigin`'s
#   `nua` in a sorted column where the missing bit is the first thing the eye lands on.
#
# An admitted bit never set is a question
#   Sometimes it is a defect. `StatedFit` admitted `nua` while `remainder sign` exercised only
#   `.ua`, and the element's own annotation refuses the missing bit in prose: overlapping ranges
#   are a `transition` fit, which the value arm names. The mask is what sets the two side by side.
#   A word in a sorted column is a comparison a reader makes at a glance; a pile of annotations is
#   not.
#
# The masks cluster
#   That is structure rather than trivia. Sort by the word and the wrappers fall into a handful of
#   kinds. Two questions with one mask are the same kind of question; a mask that is a strict
#   subset of another is a candidate for the narrower type. A subset is a candidate and never a
#   verdict: a site may simply be young. The reading is "go and look at this one", which is what an
#   observation is for.
#
# It does not know what is admissible
#   It knows only what was taken. The admissible word lives in the XSD (`pm:Absence` is `nua`,
#   `pm:ClaimAbsence` is `.ua`) and in this database as the `a_..._absence_has_no_none` CHECKs.
#   Comparing the two is the reader's job, and stating that plainly is better than a relation that
#   guesses at a grammar it cannot see.
#
# A derivation is not a bit
#   It is not an absence: it names the identity that computes the position, and
#   epistemics/derivations.sqlc counts it.
-- epistemics/absences.sqlc folded to one three-bit word per question.
SELECT a.question,
       (CASE WHEN bool_or(a.reason = 'none')          THEN 'n' ELSE '.' END) ||
       (CASE WHEN bool_or(a.reason = 'unmeasured')    THEN 'u' ELSE '.' END) ||
       (CASE WHEN bool_or(a.reason = 'notApplicable') THEN 'a' ELSE '.' END) AS mask,
       count(*)                                                             AS filings,
       count(*) FILTER (WHERE a.reason = 'none')                            AS as_none
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/absences.sqlc)
) a
WHERE a.reason IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY a.question
